

Prim's vs Dijkstra (Side by Side)

Use this graph:

      100
   A ------- B
   |         |
  40        40
   |         |
   C ------- D
       40
What is each algorithm trying to optimize?
Dijkstra	Prim's
Shortest distance from source A to every vertex	Minimum total cost to connect all vertices
Thinks about paths	Thinks about a tree
Source matters	Source doesn't matter
The question being asked
Dijkstra
"What is the cheapest way to reach B from A?"
"What is the cheapest way to reach C from A?"
"What is the cheapest way to reach D from A?"
Prim's
"How can I connect A, B, C, D
with the minimum total edge cost?"
